  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Tuesday)\nIssued at 133 PM MDT Tue Sep 29 2026\n\nCurrent Water Vapor and upper air models show shortwave just east\nof the forecast area and an upper low over the four corners\nregion, with northwest flow over us. 19Z surface analysis shows\nfrontal boundary associated with the wave over far eastern SD this\nafternoon. Mostly clear skies sit over the area, with \ntemperatures in the 70s and light winds out of the west to \nnorthwest. Some patchy areas of fog and low ceilings is possible\novernight into Wednesday morning, generally for eastern SD, \nhowever could impact south-central SD. Little change to the \noverall pattern is expected through the week, with northwest flow \naloft hanging around. Mostly dry conditions are expected as well. \nA cold front is expected Thursday, dropping temperatures from the \nmid-70s down into the 60s, and bringing a small chance for some \nlight precipitation into the area. A couple weak impulses move \nthrough the northern plains over the weekend and early next week, \nhowever models currently show little to no moisture associated \nwith these waves.",
